  "why": "B21. Every call goes through a receiver whose type is written down: an interface-typed field (lands on the interface member, D2), a property, a parameter, a typed local, `var v = new Store()`, a field inherited from the base class, `this._store2`, a static call on an in-repo type (D5), and a member the receiver's type inherits (found on the nearest declaring type, D4). The interface lives in a sibling namespace reached by `using`, so `Store : IStore` is itself a case: the per-file pass placed the base in `App.Data` and the fallback made it an external `csharp:IStore`.",
